From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slothfulchat <patches@slothfulchat.invalid>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:06:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 86/92] web-app: say why a download failed and what to do about
 it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Core gives a post-message that no relay has yet ten minutes before failing
it, because its sender may still be uploading a large attachment
(core/0034). The UI cannot see why a download failed, but the message's
age says which cause is likely, and a bare "download failed" helped with
neither:

- Received within the hour: most likely still uploading — "May still be
  arriving — try again in a few minutes".
- Older: most likely deleted from the relay (chatmail relays clear
  messages out after a while) or never arrived, which a retry cannot fix —
  "Not found on your relay — ask the sender to send it again", or "… send it
  again from your other device" for your own message from another device.

The retry button stays in every case, for the rarer causes a retry does
fix. One `DownloadFailedLabel` component replaces the four "download failed"
spans in the download placeholder and the one in Message.tsx's plain
fallback. The strings are fork-only and go into _untranslated_en.json.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
